-- aar/w3/aar_row_654_draft1.sql. DRAFT 1 by W3 (session_01H1X3ANsGiMnhnbkfphocmo) for the coordinator (seat 36). NOT RUN by W3.
-- One ask_aar_snapshots row for ASK 654 (the Oracle takes a pressed verse itself through the four layers) and its ask_aar_builders row.
-- Every value is from Wall 12176 to 12242 under root 12065 (the posts named in sources, read by W3), ask654/w3/plan654.md rev 11, W4's b3 files (ply_lines.js, blockA.txt, close1d.txt, t654b3_out.txt, read whole by W3), W4's card and the message above it and the press record (read by W3 in W4's thread by message id), the operator's messages in W3's thread, and md5sum by W3 of the files named.
-- NOT READ by W3: the audit_log row; the live engine and n8n; W1's grade files in git; the b1 and b2 test outputs.
-- HOLD: the third grades entry needs the Wall id of W1's post that states the written target's md5 in full (token W1FULLMD5WALL below). Draft 2 fills it. Do not insert draft 1.
-- objective_met is 'in part': written and read back; no run since the write.
